[{:seon.task/name "vectors-clean-is-a-commit"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: `seon.vector/round` keeps :clean, the db at which everything due was asked, so the next round embeds only `seon.vector/written` between it and main (a datoms-diff); under churn it pins a stale version, and the :embedded ask carries a db too. Correct: :clean and the :embedded ask keep {:t :commit}, and round makes the base with d/commit-as-db before `written` (the diff reads the same nodes). Replaces the db values in the proc's state with references (AGENTS section 4). Cost: one more call per round; `seon.vector-cost-test/a-commit-is-embedded-for-what-it-changed` moves by the measured delta."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/needs #{"seon.writer/main-notices-carry-a-commit-not-a-db"}
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.vector-cost-test/a-commit-is-embedded-for-what-it-changed seon.vector-test/a-caught-up-round-diffs-from-its-clean-commit}}
 {:seon.task/name "the-model-is-loaded-outside-root"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: the :embed effect (resources/seon/system.edn: {:perform seon.vector/embed :open seon.vector/open :workers 1}) runs on a worker thread in root, and `seon.vector/open` loads llama.cpp, the 310 MB gguf (:seon.config.vector/model) and Metal into root at its first batch, where they stay. Measured 2026-10-29 on a scratch root: an idle root that had embedded once was 1,590 MB footprint, one that had not 1,106 MB (the gguf mapped 384 MB resident, the Metal driver loaded); a crash in llama.cpp or Metal is root's crash. Owner, 2026-10-29: \"Can't the embedding happen in a separate fork of main? Can't we offload it to its own agent and a flow process?\" Correct: the vectors proc stays in root and asks as now; the :embed kind's worker is a process the fork server forks (as it forks agents and test children: copy-on-write program, its own memory), which loads the model, answers batches over its socket and ends when no batch waits (its end is EOF and its exit a fact; no clock); a failure is :seon.vector/* error data to the vectors proc. Measured 2026-10-29 (three boots of one resumed scratch store, idle 120 s): model loaded 1,641 MB footprint and 224 MB malloc, never loaded (SEON_EMBED_TEXTS=0) 1,262 MB and 7.5 MB; of the malloc 206 MB is llama.cpp and Metal from seon_embed_open once (the tokenizer's vocabulary 83.5 MB in 787 k blocks, ggml_backend_sched_new 66.9 MB, Metal's shader cache 30 MB), no leak seen; :seon.config.vector/batch-tokens 4096 also maps 721 MB of virtual Metal buffers (210 MB at 1024, about 160 MB less footprint and about 5% less throughput, one sample each); the load takes about 4 s. A search (an eval of related text) embeds its query too, so the child serves queries as well as batches, and a search on an idle root waits for the load. Measure first: the model's load time in a fresh process (decides whether a worker lives per batch or while batches keep coming), and whether the fork server forks such a child with what it has. Replaces the in-root worker; adds no runner (an effect whose worker is a child is the fork server's existing mechanism). Waits for the owner's go on the plan (a change to how an effect runs). Measure root's footprint after embedding, before and after."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.vector-test/root-holds-no-model-after-an-embed}}]
